  "question": {
    "text": "For the natural numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo></math> is equal to:",
